. It seemed like it took forever to get through the haunted house witch makes it worth the wait. There’s no lines on the in side of the haunted house. The mazes you go through lasted long enough to enjoy everything. Love the skull head wall. They looked like they were floating. Love the spinning tunnel!!! It was worth the 2 hour drive.\nL234: I Dare you to try and scare them lol but beware you might get a knife thrown at your head. Lol yes a real knife. I love scaring people. I think I pissed that lady off lol\nL235: October 2019\nL236: \nL237: Fun Factor  |\nL238: Haunt Value  |\nL239: Scare Factor  |\nL240: \nL241: Was this review helpful? [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL242: \nL243: 1 out of 2 people found this review helpful\nL244: \nL245: WAS THE BEST ONE IN THE AREA\nL246: \nL247: I like the way they made the rooms and pennywise was very good at scarring me the way he ran around in the room he was quick just like in the movie and how he was hitting his head on the glass felt so real great job will be coming back next year his laugh is by far the best I’ve heard.\nL248: \nL249: October 2019\nL250: Fun Factor  |\nL251: Haunt Value  |\nL252: Scare Factor  |\nL253: \nL254: Was this review helpful? [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL255: \nL256: 0 out of 1 person found this review helpful\nL257: \nL258: Absolutely loved it\nL259: Absolutely loved it! Wolfmans is clearly among the best haunted houses in the state. Lots of things have changed since last year. Attention to detail was awesome. The scares were of good quality. In fact, it had some of the creepiest and best pop out scares I'd ever encountered. My nieces screamed in many places in the haunt. I was also startled by few of the scares. Actors all did a great job. Ticket rates to the haunt was affordable. I will come again.\nL260: \nL261: November 2018\nL262: Fun Factor  |\nL263: Haunt Value  |\nL264: Scare Factor  |\nL265: \nL266: Was this review helpful? [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL267: \nL268: 2 out of 4 people found this review helpful\nL269: \nL270: Incredible scenes\nL271: \nL272: VERIFIED\nL273: It was a two hour’s drive from my place. But the haunt did not disappoint us. We were made to wait for hours in the line as well. Once inside we could feel the eeriness. The house was well designed and looks very much haunted. It was one huge maze of rooms which was filled with scares. It made me jump a few times and scream at the top of my voice. Props were used extensively and that added to the creepiness. Actors put up a good show. They were brilliant and showcased incredible scenes with ease.\nL274: Had an amazingly good time and love to return back.\nL275: October 2018\nL276: \nL277: Fun Factor  |\nL278: Haunt Value  |\nL279: Scare Factor  |\nL280: \nL281: Was this review helpful? [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL282: \nL283: 1 out of 2 people found this review helpful\nL284: \nL285: One of the best spook house\nL286: \nL287: VERIFIED\nL288: We were a group of six people and we had a blast @ Wolfmans. It is one of the best spook houses I have been to. The set design was creepy at best. Lots of scares. I am not scared too easily. But few of the scares caught me totally off guard. My GF got freaked out by the guy in the demon mask. It was also family friendly. Staff was helpful throughout. Recommend this place.\nL289: \nL290: October 2018\nL291: \nL292: Fun Factor  |\nL293: Haunt Value  |\nL294: Scare Factor  |\nL295: \nL296: Was this review helpful? [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL297: 0 out of 1 person found this review helpful\nL298: \nL299: cite69†View All 30 Reviews L300: \nL301: * * *\nL302: ## Share Your Experience\nL303: \nL304: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL305: \nL306: Overall Rating *\nL307: \nL308: Click to rate\nL309: \nL310: Review Title * [Input]\nL311: \nL312: No caps or profanity\nL313: \nL314: Your Review *\nL315: \nL316: Your Name [Input]\nL317: \nL318: Optional\nL319: \nL320: Email Address * [Input]\nL321: \nL322: For verification only, will